@@ -8908,3 +8908,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-10: GAP-4 PRE-REGISTERED PRECISION CONFIRMATION v3 (THE confirmatory experiment, owed for 2 milestones -- it MUST EXECUTE this time): k=3 ALL-FRESH chains (no probe/stale arms), equal 600s timeouts, on NEW clean chain-feasible ARC-2 tasks, protocol committed BEFORE any call. PRIMARY gate = binomial critical-value rule: n>=19 agreement events, reject H0 p=0.52 if >=14 gold (size 0.046, power 0.837 at p=0.80). SECONDARY = precision vs the in-run fresh-arm base rate (~0.73). EXECUTION-FLOOR (the .370 fix): the artifact is INVALID unless total_codex_calls>0 AND n_agreement_events>0 -- it CANNOT emit pending_execution; if codex cannot run, emit blocked_codex_unavailable. Honest verdict either way; retire_if_same_verdict -- if the agreement signal AGAIN fails to clear 0.52 with power (or again fails to execute), the agreement-as-selector claim is retired and agreement is logged as confidence-label-only. EXCLUDE the flagged reuse tasks aa4ec2a5/16b78196 from the clean set. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_execution_floor_unmet; results/experiment_4009_gap4_precision_confirmation_v3.json
 - 2026-06-10: GAP-5 CROSS-EXAMPLE-CONSISTENCY SELECTOR upgrade (build against the logged GAP-5 demo-underdetermination gap per the Missing-Verifier Gap Logging mandate): exp4001 logged GAP-5 (multiple demo-consistent programs disagree on the test = the verifier cannot select among them). Build a STRONGER discriminator than plain output-agreement: among induced demo-perfect programs, score each by (a) cross-DEMONSTRATION consistency (does it reproduce held-out demo pairs, leave-one-demo-out) and (b) SIBLING-INPUT agreement (do the candidate programs agree on perturbed/sibling inputs). Measure whether this lifts precision and/or coverage over plain final-grid output-agreement on the SAME ARC-2 chain-feasible pool (reuse the cached induced programs; NO new codex calls if the saved programs suffice). The cleanest off-the-shelf design (arXiv:2604.02434 cross-example consistency filtering). A new registry-eligible discriminator that closes a logged gap is direct progress on Carnot's core. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: gap5_cross_example_no_better_than_agreement_coverage_lower; results/experiment_4010_gap5_cross_example_consistency_selector.json
 - 2026-06-11: GAP-4 DECENTRALIZATION via BEST-OF-N local sampling (close the .370 induction gap; the BARC regime): replace exp4002's weak <=3-attempt generic-GGUF arm (25.81% induction, pass@2=vote) with k=8-16 INDEPENDENT local samples per task from a SOTA LOCAL GGUF (unsloth/gemma-4-12B-it-GGUF preferred for throughput; gemma-4-26B-A4B fallback), each filtered by the FREE demo-fit verifier (exact-demo-reproduction gate, ~0.11s/task). Re-run the GAP-4 venue on the SAME ARC-1 31-task pool: best-of-N local induces def transform(grid) from demo pairs only -> model-free verifier (demo-fit + restricted-namespace execution + content-hash match) reranks. Report the best-of-N local induction demo-perfect COVERAGE (target: approach codex 0.94, vs the <=3-attempt 0.2581), gated rerank pass@2 vs vote 0.4516 / oracle 0.6129 / codex 0.5806, AND the COST (local-generator seconds vs codex seconds; the verifier is ~free). The decentralization-clean, sovereign efficiency path: more local compute + free filtering. No published work reports local-open-weight ARC induction with execution-verifier reranking. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: gap4_local_bestofn_cov0.2581_pass20.4516_below_codex; results/experiment_4012_gap4_local_best_of_n.json
+- 2026-06-11: EFFICIENCY axis (north-star §5) -- model-free verifier vs LLM-judge cost ratio ON ARC selection: head-to-head on the SAME candidate sets from the ARC-1/ARC-2 pools, (A) the model-free GAP-4 verifier (demo-fit + restricted-namespace execution + content-hash match, ~0.11s/task) selects the best candidate; (B) an LLM-judge (codex/gpt-5.5) selects from the identical candidate set. Report SELECTION-ACCURACY PARITY (do A and B pick the same / equally-gold candidate, within CI) AND the COMPUTE/LATENCY RATIO (verifier seconds + tokens vs judge seconds + tokens) -- the 'parity at Nx cheaper' claim. This is the cleanest statement of 'the verifier earns its place on cost' in the ARC venue; no published work reports an apples-to-apples model-free-verifier-vs-LLM-judge cost ratio on ARC. The model-free verifier is the cheap, hardware-acceleratable, externally-grounded forward-pass primitive (north-star §5). (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: verifier_parity_at_95.3x_cheaper_than_judge; results/experiment_4013_verifier_vs_judge_efficiency.json
